# Whisipedia background work (orchestrator, index builds, ad-hoc jobs started with tools/wsp-bg):
# one shared memory, swap, CPU and IO budget, so that however many jobs run at once, the desktop keeps
# the rest of the machine. The API is not in this slice; it has its own small limits.
#
# Budget for a 16 GiB WSL (the workstation's .wslconfig since 2026-10-11; the API takes up to 5 GiB of
# the rest): MemoryHigh throttles (reclaims) the slice before
# MemoryMax is reached; MemoryMax makes the kernel OOM-kill inside the slice only, never the desktop
# or the API. MemorySwapMax keeps a runaway job from pushing the whole machine into swap (the
# 2026-10-11 index build reached 21 GB RSS and 41 GB of swap). Override per machine with a drop-in:
#   systemctl --user edit whisipedia-background.slice
#
# Template: `wsp service install` renders this file (docs/runbooks/install-services.md).

[Unit]
Description=Whisipedia background work (shared memory, CPU and IO budget)

[Slice]
MemoryHigh=7G
MemoryMax=9G
MemorySwapMax=2G
CPUWeight=20
IOWeight=20
TasksMax=512
